---
import Callout from '../Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../CodeBlock.astro';
import StepCard from '../StepCard.astro';
---

<div class="sec" id="s4">
  <div class="num">04</div>
  <h2>Delta as home base</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Delta is where you should spend most of your time. Claude Code does the
    work, Delta is where you watch, review and share it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Delta (<a href="https://delta.dev">delta.dev</a>) comes from the team behind
    the Zed editor. It is built for exactly the loop from section one: you ask,
    an agent works, you review. Each task lives in a thread, which keeps the
    conversation with the agent and the code changes it made together in one
    place, so you can scroll back and see why something changed.
  </p>
  <div class="card" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
    <div>
      <div
        style="font-family: VT323, Courier New, monospace; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.1; color: var(--color-7dffa8)"
      >
        Experiments cannot wreck the original
      </div><p style="color: var(--color-9ee6b5)">
        Delta works in a separate copy of the project for each thread. If a
        thread goes sideways you close it and the original is untouched.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div
        style="font-family: VT323, Courier New, monospace; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.1; color: var(--color-7dffa8)"
      >
        Comment on the exact spot
      </div><p style="color: var(--color-9ee6b5)">
        You can leave a comment on a specific line of code or a specific message
        in the conversation to ask for a change. "Make this heading bigger"
        pointed at the heading beats describing it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div
        style="font-family: VT323, Courier New, monospace; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.1; color: var(--color-7dffa8)"
      >
        Share a thread link with me
      </div><p style="color: var(--color-9ee6b5)">
        Every thread has a link. Send it to me and I can open it, read what
        happened and help, without you having to explain anything over the
        phone.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div
        style="font-family: VT323, Courier New, monospace; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.1; color: var(--color-7dffa8)"
      >
        Claude Code stays the engine
      </div><p style="color: var(--color-9ee6b5)">
        Your Claude Code sessions can sync into Delta threads. Nothing about how
        the agent works changes. Delta gives it a home with history, comments
        and sharing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <Callout title={'Delta is new'} warning
    ><svg
      slot="icon"
      width="22"
      height="22"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      stroke="var(--color-ffb347)"
      stroke-width="2"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
      ><path d="M12 9v4"></path><path d="M12 17h.01"></path><path
        d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"
      ></path></svg
    ><p>
      It is in public beta, so things will keep changing. If the sign up flow on
      delta.dev looks different from what I describe, follow <a
        href="https://delta.dev/docs">delta.dev/docs</a
      >. If anything in Delta is not working for you yet, everything in this
      guide still works with Claude Code and Zed on their own.
    </p></Callout
  >
  <h3>Your first thread</h3>
  <div class="steps">
    <StepCard number="1" title={'Open your project'}
      ><p>
        Start Delta and open the same project folder you used with Claude Code.
        If Delta asks to connect Claude Code, say yes.
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="2" title={'Start a thread and ask for one small change'}
      ><p>
        Something you can check in ten seconds. "Change the heading to my full
        name" is perfect. Ask for a plan first.
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="3" title={'Read the plan, then read the change'}
      ><p>
        Delta shows the conversation and the files that changed side by side.
        Look at the before and after. Does it match what you asked for?
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="4" title={'Comment where it is wrong'}
      ><p>
        Click the line or the message, leave a comment saying what you want
        instead and let the agent have another go.
      </p></StepCard
    >
    <StepCard number="5" title={'Accept it'}
      ><p>
        When you are happy, accept the change so it lands in the real project.
        Then start a new thread for the next thing.
      </p></StepCard
    >
  </div>
  <CodeBlock
    label={'A good first request'}
    code={'In index.html, change the heading text to my full name and make the background colour a touch warmer. Show me a plan first and wait for my ok.'}
    copy
  />
</div>
